  "current_evidence_state": "The previous original-model, three local-model and annotation-reference comparisons are retained. A saved-prediction audit reproduces all six baseline matrix cells and 240 per-image rows. The proposed method detects every complete reviewed front but misses 13 one-corner and five zero-corner fronts; its 51 extras comprise five duplicates, 36 nearby unmatched and ten low-overlap unmatched predictions. These geometric bands are not physical verdicts. A fixed reflected-view output-anchor probe reduces reviewed misses/extras to 15/43 with unchanged pair counts, doubles duplicates to ten, and loses corner successes under both older references; it is not promoted. The accepted-pair diagnostic separates 569 supported successes from all 678 emitted pairs. Both prepared paired training experiments remain pending. Future unseen-group claims must exclude held groups from starting-weight history as well as fine-tuning. The upstream baomai guidance specifies two independently available corner slots but no downstream interface or physical acceptance tolerance; the report records those requirements as unspecified.",
